        "job": "Make tiles of my Marketplace tools and workflows, each with its own icon drawn, for a page or a film to show",
        "description": "Reads the tools and workflows as the shelf's readers answer them (two JSON files of { items: [{ id, kind, title, job, steps?, icon? }] }) and the icons folder of an installed lucide-react, and answers one tile per item: id, kind, title, job (cut to 90 characters), steps, icon and svg, the icon's own shape elements (the item's icon, else its kind's icon from marketplace-kinds.json; an alias icon file is followed). Titles that read as machine names are left out. With --out it writes window.<global>=<tiles>; for a page (global TILES unless --global names another). The icon files are read as data, never run. Last line: {\"result\": {tiles, counts}} or {\"error\": ...}.",
